{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"vaporish-germicidal-chamois","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nChanges 1031 (228b: DET-floor short-circuit, c781127a2) and 1035 (7e77: BLOCK-verdict reuse, 517e0470a) are individually green but semantically interact: tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py::test_force_bypasses_verdict_reuse and ::test_code_change_reruns_full_review assert the full review invokes the finder (calls > 0), but their fixture plans do not pass the deterministic floor (P1 AC checklist), so the now-landed short-circuit returns a BLOCK with zero finder calls. Main is red for every subsequent change whose tree contains both commits (observed: Verified -1 on 1041, 1039, 1040). CI run: 30540561663.\n\n## Approach\nFix the test fixtures, not the code: give the two tests' fixture plans a DET-floor-passing shape (a `## Acceptance Criteria` checklist with valid items) so a bypassed/invalidated reuse genuinely reaches the LLM passes, preserving each test's intent (--force reruns the full review; a code change reruns the full review). Audit the rest of test_plan_review_reuse.py for the same latent assumption. No production code changes.\n\n## Scope\ntests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py\n\n## Testing\nThe two failing tests pass with the finder invoked; the full tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py suite passes; a spot-run of tests/unit/workflow/test_det_short_circuit.py confirms no regression.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] test_force_bypasses_verdict_reuse and test_code_change_reruns_full_review pass on a tree containing both c781127a2 and 517e0470a (checked: `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py`).\n- [ ] All other tests in the file pass unmodified in intent (checked: same pytest run).","id":"2c38-bef7-b045-4ecc","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"reuse tests break under DET short-circuit (post-1031/1035 main)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785422750073713001,"uuid":"3617e3b4-5e22-4233-aadc-e7c9f21d9c3c"}